<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 18 January, from 1535 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1535 CE <span class="tih-ago">491 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francisco Pizarro founds Lima</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pizarro founded the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">City of Kings</a>' on the Rímac river near the Pacific coast. Lima became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>, created in 1542, and the centre of Spanish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1654 CE <span class="tih-ago">372 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pereiaslav Council places the Cossack Hetmanate under the Tsar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> officers swore allegiance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexis-of-russia">Tsar Alexei</a> in return for protection against Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. The agreement's meaning remains disputed in Ukrainian and Russian history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1778 CE <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Cook becomes the first European to sight Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his third voyage, Cook sighted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oahu</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kauai">Kauai</a>, where he landed two days later. He named the archipelago the Sandwich Islands and was killed there in February 1779.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1871 CE <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wilhelm I proclaimed German Emperor at Versailles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> still under siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>'s king was proclaimed Emperor of a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Bismarck's creation dominated continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> until 1918.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">Wilhelm I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 CE <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan presents its Twenty-One Demands to China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> secretly pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>'s government for extensive rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and beyond. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> accepted a reduced version under ultimatum, fuelling Chinese nationalism against Japan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet forces open a land corridor into besieged Leningrad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Iskra, Soviet troops linked up south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, creating a narrow corridor into Leningrad after 16 months of siege. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> was finally lifted in January 1944.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1958 CE <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Willie O'Ree breaks the NHL colour barrier</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Playing for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Bruins against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> Canadiens, Willie O'Ree became the first Black player in the National Hockey League, despite being almost blind in one eye.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li></ol>
